---
description: Save & Spend autonomous development and review-gate rules
alwaysApply: true
---

Read `AGENTS.md` before doing any work. Treat it as the governing contract.

Read `.agent/state.json` and `backlog/tasks.json` at the beginning and end of every turn. If projectStatus is `awaiting_initial_review`, do not implement product code; only answer review questions or improve the harness if explicitly asked.

When projectStatus is `active`, follow the complete autonomous loop in `AGENTS.md`. Select the highest-priority task that is todo and unblocked. Do not stop after a single feature: plan, build, test, browser-validate where required, request a read-only verifier subagent, perform the mandatory harness-evolution audit, fix findings, update state, commit, and continue.

When `autonomyMode` is `usability_evolution`, also follow `docs/USABILITY_LOOP.md`. Operate and critique the UI as a novice user, create the next evidence-backed task yourself, and repeat until two consecutive independent audits are clean. Do not wait for the human to identify tasks or accept vague self-praise as review evidence.

Run `npm run validate` before marking any task done. Never claim success if it fails. Never weaken tests or documented constraints to pass validation.

Autonomously strengthen engineering constraints, tests, validation, observability, documentation, and agent rules whenever evidence supports it. Record every such change in `docs/HARNESS_EVOLUTION.md`. Do not change protected product policy or weaken a guardrail; those require a genuine human decision.

Only ask the human for a protected product-policy decision or a genuine blocker that has exhausted the documented retry policy. Record the blocker with reproducible evidence before stopping.
